      "id": 1,
      "text": "Pinetop–Lakeside was founded in 1984 when the neighboring towns of Pinetop and Lakeside merged.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinetop-Lakeside%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Early Mormon settlers moved into the area around Pinetop–Lakeside in the mid‑1880s, becoming the primary non‑native residents for much of its early history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinetop-Lakeside%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from two origins: Lakeside from its lakes, and Pinetop from saloon owner Walt Rigney’s nickname tied to his tall saloon building.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinetop-Lakeside%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2002, the Rodeo–Chediski Fire threatened Pinetop–Lakeside and forced an evacuation of the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinetop-Lakeside%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Pinetop–Lakeside’s primary industry in its early days was sawmills that harvested the surrounding mature Ponderosa Pine forests.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinetop-Lakeside%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Pinetop–Lakeside is a popular summer resort and second‑home area for Arizona desert residents.",
